# ADD OS — line-ending handling.
#
# Deliberately scoped to one path. This repo has no repo-wide `text=auto` rule and
# this file does not add one: changing normalisation for every tracked file is a
# separate decision with a much larger blast radius, and nothing here needs it.
#
# The pinned API contract is the exception, because byte-identity IS its contract.
# `pnpm api:collection:check` (scripts/check-api-collection.js) hashes the
# WORKING-TREE bytes of this snapshot and of the canonical file in ADDCore, and
# docs/api/README.md records a sha256 for the pin. With `core.autocrlf=true` — which
# is the setting on the machine this was pinned from — a fresh checkout rewrites LF
# to CRLF, changing those bytes and making the guard report a mismatch that has
# nothing to do with the API contract having moved. `-text` disables all conversion
# for this path, so what is committed is what lands on disk, on every platform.
docs/api/ADD-OS.postman_collection.json -text
